{"id": "1d16f0dd-2473-47b2-b805-258d729c7b28", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T18:56:15.840516", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "f846af60-0824-4a72-ba53-52695e471546", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-d0dae33b-a78e-42ed-837c-0ca5937df24e", "tool_call": {"id": "call-d0dae33b-a78e-42ed-837c-0ca5937df24e", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Submit design plan for BAdam perturbation analysis\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"## 1. Repository inspection (evidence)\\n- `/workspace` contains only `task.json` (699 B). No source files, no notes about BAdam/Adam, no fine-tuning scripts, no datasets, no models.\\n- No `BAdam`/`badam`/`block_aware` strings anywhere except inside the task question inside `task.json`.\\n- `task.json.documents.track.md` is referenced but the file does not exist on disk. The task's own `context` field states: \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"\\n- Environment (from runtime): Python 3.12.3 only generic packages (no torch / transformers / numpy / scipy), `gpu_enabled: false`, 24 CPU cores, 125 GiB RAM, ~696 GB free on /workspace, network disabled.\\n- No compute budget, GPU budget or task specification is stated beyond the question itself.\\n\\n## 2. High-level design (NOT executed — design only)\\n- **Nominate models/tasks.** Default ladder: (a) `pythia-160m` + SST-2 (cheap), (b) `TinyLlama-1.1B` + SQuAD-v1.1 (standard), (c) `Llama-3.2-3B` QLoRA + WikiText-103 (stretch). Final selection deferred to researcher.\\n- **Modules to instrument.** Per layer ℓ: `q_proj`, `k_proj`, `v_proj`, `o_proj` (separately so Q/K/V can be analysed), `up_proj`, `gate_proj`, `down_proj`; plus `embed_tokens.W` and `lm_head`. Layer-norm and bias tracked via histogram, not SVD.\\n- **Capture of Δθ.** Live `optimizer.step()` pre/post snapshots -> Δθ = θ_{t+1} − θ_t. Replay from `(m_t, v_t)` as cross-check. Sample every k steps (default k=5) to bound storage.\\n- **Heavy-tail metrics.** Power-law shape α via MLE on σ/σ_1 (Clauset–Newman), KS distance, excess kurtosis of log σ, log-log spectral decay slope β on the tail, Hill tail index γ as robustness.\\n- **Effective rank.** Roy–Vetterli erank = exp(H(p)), plus α-erank for α∈{0.5,1,2}, plus numerically stable rank r_ε for ε∈{1e-1,1e-3,1e-6}.\\n- **Controls.** Adam/AdamW (reference, required), BAdam (subject, required), SGD-momentum 0.9 (optional), LoRA-Adam (rank 4/8/16 on the same W, optional), random sign-matched Δθ of equal ‖·‖_F (null, recommended). Each run = (model, dataset) × seed × optimizer.\\n- **Seeds & statistics.** ≥5 seeds per (optimizer, module), matched data order per seed. 5–10 step-buckets for non-stationarity. 95 % bootstrap CIs, paired Wilcoxon + Cliff's δ for Adam vs BAdam, two-way ANOVA (module × optimizer), TOST equivalence on erank with pre-registered ±10 % margin, BH-FDR across modules.\\n- **Analysis plan.** (i) per-step SVD -> metrics, (ii) stationarity plots of erank and α, (iii) optimizer comparisons per module, (iv) module-dependence heat-maps, (v) H1 verdict per (module, step) cell with goodness-of-fit thresholds, (vi) TOST equivalence verdict.\\n- **Pre-registered decision rule.** A module is \\\"Adam-like\\\" iff (a) α_BAdam falls in Adam's bootstrap CI AND (b) |erank_BAdam − erank_Adam|/erank_Adam ≤ 0.10 with TOST p<0.025. Direction + effect size reported otherwise.\\n\\n## 3. Assumptions (separated from fixed requirements)\\n1. BAdam ≡ block-coordinate Adam: one block of params updated per global step with Adam moments; the rest frozen. Block size/schedule are design hyperparameters.\\n2. Δθ is taken from raw parameter snapshots, not from m̂/(√v̂+ε); replay is only a cross-check.\\n3. Step alignment = one logical step per complete sweep over all BAdam blocks; per-substep metrics are reported as a secondary table.\\n4. σ values are normalized by ‖Δθ‖_F when computing α, κ, β; raw σ reported alongside as sensitivity.\\n5. SVD only on 2-D weights; 1-D params (LN, biases) handled separately by sorted-|entries|.\\n\\n## 4. Uncertainties requiring clarification before I deliver the full design\\n1. Which BAdam paper/implementation defines it here (Luo et al. 2024 ICLR vs other)? Block size and block schedule.\\n2. Base model and size (Pythia-160M / TinyLlama-1.1B / LLaMA-3.2-3B / other).\\n3. Fine-tuning task and dataset.\\n4. Compute budget and GPU availability (env says CPU-only, network disabled — must confirm).\\n5. Whether mandatory dependencies (`torch`, `transformers`, `numpy`, `scipy`, `powerlaw`, optional `transformer_optimal_eig gesn`) may be installed offline, or whether SVD/erank/MLE power-law must be implemented from scratch in stdlib.\\n6. Whether SGD and LoRA baselines are in scope or excluded.\\n7. Allowed snapshot sampling granularity (CPU feasibility).\\n8. Whether Q proj biases and tied embeddings/lm_head are tracked.\\n9. Whether analysis happens during training (streaming metrics) or only post-hoc.\",\"evidence\":\"/workspace contains only task.json (699 B); no code, configs, notes or data; `track.md` referenced but missing; environment shows Python 3.12 without ML packages, GPU disabled, 24 CPUs, 125 GiB RAM, network disabled; task.json explicit context says \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\\\".\",\"assumptions\":\"1. BAdam treated as block-coordinate Adam at the parameter-block level (subject to researcher override with a named paper). 2. Δθ captured from raw parameter snapshots, replayed from optimizer state only as cross-check. 3. Logical step = full sweep over BAdam blocks; per-substep stats recorded separately. 4. Singular values normalized by ‖Δθ‖_F when measuring shape, while raw version is kept as sensitivity. 5. SVD applied only to 2-D weights; 1-D params (LN, bias) handled by sorted-|entries|. 6. Power-law fits use MLE with left truncation; fits with σ_max/σ_min<10 flagged as inconclusive.\",\"uncertainties\":\"1. Identidad concreta del paper/implementación de BAdam, block size y block schedule. 2. Modelo base y tamaño. 3. Tarea de fine-tuning y dataset. 4. Presupuesto computacional y disponibilidad de GPU (entorno declara gpu_enabled:false, network disabled). 5. Stack de bibliotecas permitido (torch, transformers, numpy, scipy, powerlaw, transformer_optimal_eig gesn) — instalación offline vs implementación propia. 6. Inclusión/exclusión de SGD y LoRA-Adam como controles. 7. Frecuencia de captura de snapshots factible en CPU. 8. Inclusión de sesgos de atención y de embeddings/lm_head atadas. 9. Análisis in-training vs sólo post-hoc.\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-dd74a505-7526-4230-a86d-cf8f06fd1136", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 14}
